+// The toolbar switch (maintainer, 2026-10-04: "easy to find and quite prominent", in the empty space between the
+// address bar and the extension and menu buttons). It shows its name and the level in use in words; a click opens
+// the three levels, each with the same long explanation on hover as in Settings. The words are in
+// browser/gorillaSatellite.ftl, which Settings reads too. It is created when the first window is about to show,
+// not at browser-before-ui-startup: loading CustomizableUI that early would run before BrowserGlue's UI migrations
+// edit the toolbar layout pref. A user who removes it keeps it removed (CustomizableUI remembers seen widgets, and
+// PLACED_PREF stops the one-time move next to the address bar from happening again).
